BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Title: Adjust the retrieval machinery, not just the final wording) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Body: These implementation choices come directly from the practitioners' demonstrations and working) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (preferences.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (Items: Use a reranker to inspect more candidate knowledge while sending only a few high-relevance chunks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (to the answering model. Medin uses this in almost every RAG implementation. [Cole Medin - tLMViADvSNE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (@ 00:02:17]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (Keep existing entities available during graph extraction. Neo4j describes passing known products, partners,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (clients, or other structured entities into the prompt so the model recognizes them and extracts relationships.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm ([AI Engineer - XNneh6-eyPg @ 00:11:00]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (Tune the similarity cutoff against known cases. Case Resolver's team measured relevant and unrelated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (match scores before drawing the dividing line. [Mirketa Inc - 8N3k2qP_0SY @ 00:30:10]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (After changing the embedding model in Open WebUI, reimport the documents. Professor Patterns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (demonstrates uploading the directory again even though the resumes remain visible in the collection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm ([Professor Patterns - LmXaPUky_u4 @ 00:08:04]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (disagreements-and-alternatives) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 458.40 Tm (Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 436.17 Tm (IBM Technology gives long context a serious place instead of treating a vector database as mandatory. For) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 420.95 Tm (a bounded collection requiring global reasoning, such as comparing full requirements with release notes, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 405.72 Tm (speaker favors placing the documents directly in context. A search for omitted requirements can retrieve) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 390.50 Tm (matching snippets without exposing the gap between the complete documents [UabBYexBD4k @ 00:06:15].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 375.27 Tm (That simplicity has a processing trade-off: IBM's example of a 500-page manual represents roughly 250,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 360.05 Tm (tokens processed repeatedly, while RAG pays the manual's indexing cost upfront. Prompt caching partly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 344.82 Tm (offsets the repeated work for static information, not constantly changing streams [UabBYexBD4k @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 329.60 Tm (00:07:35]. Cole Medin offers an intermediate playbook through hierarchical retrieval: search small chunks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 314.37 Tm (precisely, use their metadata to identify the parent file, and return the entire document when it is small) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 299.15 Tm (enough to read [tLMViADvSNE @ 00:09:06]. Mirketa draws a different boundary altogether. For account) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 283.92 Tm (balances, case status, entitlement levels, or order numbers, Alec recommends ordinary structured database) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 268.70 Tm (queries. Semantic retrieval earns its place with nuanced documents, emails, and case notes [8N3k2qP_0SY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 253.47 Tm (@ 00:26:41]. The contrast is about the question and the data: complete-document comparison, targeted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 238.25 Tm (passage retrieval, and exact structured lookup are not the same operational job.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 223.02 Tm (Graph advocates also take different implementation paths. The Neo4j presenters describe a graph retriever) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 207.80 Tm (beginning with an index search, then following relationships from those entry points to bring back additional) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 192.57 Tm (relevant context. The starting search can be vector, full text, or another supported approach; the graph adds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 177.35 Tm (connected information rather than merely another isolated text fragment [XNneh6-eyPg @ 00:12:44].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 162.12 Tm (Writer's Sam Julien reports a historical move away from a conventional graph-database implementation after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 146.90 Tm (the team encountered scaling costs, expertise limits, and difficulties with the matching they needed. Writer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 131.67 Tm (instead stored graph-structured data points as JSON in a Lucene-based search engine, retaining) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 116.45 Tm (relationships while using infrastructure the team understood [XlAIgmi_Vow @ 00:09:42]. Adam Lucek) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 101.22 Tm (explores another distinction inside Microsoft's GraphRAG: local search gathers specific entity-linked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 86.00 Tm (information, global search works with community reports, and DRIFT combines broader community) Tj ET
